# Page surface styles

Member portal and admin pages use shared HeroUI admin shell + Card patterns.

## Admin page shell

Use [`AdminPageSurface`](src/components/AdminPageSurface.tsx) for admin routes:

```tsx
<AdminPageSurface
  title="…"
  description="…" // optional
  onManage={() => setOpen(true)} // optional → cog + Manage
  manageAriaLabel="Manage … settings"
  maxWidth="2xl" // xl | 2xl | 3xl | 5xl | full
>
  {/* body: Cards, lists, alerts, modals */}
</AdminPageSurface>
```

- Header via [`AdminPageHeader`](src/components/AdminPageHeader.tsx) (title | Manage upper right; description below)
- Manage trigger: [`AdminManageButton`](src/components/AdminManageButton.tsx) — cog + **Manage**, not “Settings”
- Put changeable page content in `children` only — do not re-hand-roll `grid max-w-* gap-6` + `h1` on admin pages

## Body surfaces

- Forms/settings sections: `Card` → `Card.Header` (`Card.Title`, `Card.Description` + `text-foreground/85`) → `Card.Content`
- Forms: HeroUI `Form`, `TextField` + `Label` + `Input`, `Select` + `ListBox`, `Button variant="primary"`
- Feedback: HeroUI `Alert` (success/danger)
- Result/list rows: `Card` / `Card.Content`

## Admin settings = modals

- No separate Admin nav routes/pages for settings
- Config lives in a modal on the parent admin page
- Old `/settings` paths redirect to parent
- Trigger via `onManage` on `AdminPageSurface` / `AdminPageHeader`

## Don't

- Raw bordered inputs / DIY `bg-blue-900` buttons when HeroUI exists
- Title+description in one flex child beside Manage (wraps button under copy)
- Label settings triggers “Settings” — use **Manage** + cog

